B)
@GeneratedValue --> how primary key will be generated
strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY/AUTO/SEQUENCE/TABLE

GenerationType.IDENTITY: Uses auto-increment in the database (common with MySQL, PostgreSQL).
GenerationType.SEQUENCE: Uses a database sequence (common with Oracle).
GenerationType.AUTO: The persistence provider will choose the appropriate strategy based on the database.
GenerationType.TABLE: Uses a table to simulate a sequence.


C)
@JoinColumn -->
The @JoinColumn annotation is used to specify the foreign key column for a relationship. This is typically used with @ManyToOne, @OneToOne, etc.


